   159	\paragraph{Mitigation.}
   160	\textbf{Keyword pruning backfired on the matched cases.} Full-context accuracy was \pruningFullAccuracy{}\%, compared with \pruningPrunedAccuracy{}\% after filtering, a change of \pruningChange{} points. Only \pruningWins{} case improved; \pruningLosses{} worsened and \pruningTies{} tied (Table~\ref{tab:pruning}). The mechanism follows from the probe design: the filter retains the competing clause because it repeats the question's words, while the paraphrased answer clause has less lexical overlap.
